# ==============================================================================
# DG-NET  —  STAGE 1: Dis-Net  (Warp Field Estimator)  +  MEAN-FRAME REFERENCE
# DTD-FSRN dataset  |  Based on Thapa et al., ICCV 2021
#
# Built on the working base script (fixed decoder skip channels, d1 in use,
# output clamp, magnitude penalty, LR 5e-5, vectorised warp stats).
#
# CHANGE vs. working base
# -----------------------
# For every video (sequence) the temporal mean of ALL its frames is computed
# once and cached to disk.  Water ripples average out, so this mean frame is a
# blurry but geometrically stable reference of the scene.  Each CNN branch now
# receives   [distorted_frame (3ch) | mean_reference (3ch)]   = 6 channels, so
# the network can estimate the ripple as the displacement of the distorted
# frame RELATIVE to a fixed reference.
#
#   * SingleFrameCNN first conv: 3 -> 6 input channels
#   * DisNet.forward(frames, ref)
#   * Dataset returns (frames, ref, wx_n, wy_n, gt, seq_id)
#   * build_ref_cache() runs once and caches (3,H,W) float16 .npy per sequence
#
# PATCH v3 — high-frequency detail (see PATCH_NOTES.md)
# -----------------------------------------------------
#   * loss_warp: removed the height round-trip terms L2/L3 (their target was ~2x
#     the GT warp and they amplified fine detail), kept L1 + multi-scale.
#   * new gradient_matching_error (+ LAMBDA_GRAD) to preserve spatial detail.
#   * magnitude penalty now acts on the UNclamped output (it was inert past the
#     clamp).  Sample plots / evaluate() now clamp like training does.
#   * extra L_G column in the log -> LOG_CSV renamed to avoid column mismatch.
#
# NOTE: checkpoints from the 3-channel model are NOT compatible, so OUT_DIR is
# different.  If SEED / TEST_SPLIT / PART_NUMBERS are unchanged you can copy
# warp_stats.json from the old checkpoints dir into the new one to skip the scan.
# ==============================================================================

